NOTE FOR MAINTAINERS: this is a minimal "all rights reserved" notice, not an
end-user license agreement. It exists because shipping with no LICENSE file
at all leaves the rights in a paid product ambiguous, which is the worse
outcome. Before Sentry is sold to the public it should have a real EULA
reviewed by a lawyer, covering at least: the terms of the paid Pro tier and
what a purchase actually grants, refunds, the Apple-required terms for any
App Store distribution, warranty disclaimers and liability limits that are
enforceable in the jurisdictions being sold into, and the relationship
between this notice and the privacy policy (docs/privacy-policy.md).
